'''Palso Thern''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] who served as a [[A/SF-01 B-wing starfighter|B-wing]] [[pilot]] in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]].<ref name="Starfighter Missions">''[[Star Wars: Starfighter Missions]]''</ref> In [[4 ABY]], he attended the briefing during which [[Chancellor (Rebel Alliance)|Chancellor]] [[Mon Mothma]] discussed the plan to attack the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station|second]] [[Death Star]] [[battle station]] over the [[Endor|Forest Moon]] of [[Endor (planet)|Endor]]. During the briefing he stood beside [[Keyan Farlander]] and other fellow pilots.<ref name="Episode VI" />

==Behind the scenes==
Palso Thern first appeared as a Rebel pilot during the briefing on ''Home One'' in [[1983]]'s [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']]. He was portrayed by an uncredited extra.<ref name="Episode VI" /> He was eventually identified and given an action figure in the "Battle Over Endor" set of [[2010]]'s ''[[Star Wars: Shadows of the Dark Side]]'', as part of ''[[Star Wars Legends]]''.<ref name="Vintage Collection">{{HasbroCite|set=Star Wars: Shadows of the Dark Side|pack=(Toys R Us Exclusive) Battle Over Endor (2 of 2)|altlink=https://www.rebelscum.com/tvcexbattleoverendor2.asp}}</ref> He was first identified in the canon continuity in [[2020]]'s ''[[Star Wars: Starfighter Missions]]'' mobile game.

